Various communities across Alberta also faced similar advisories, with additional alerts for snowfall and frigid temperatures issued for certain areas. Residents in some regions were cautioned to prepare for possible blizzard-like conditions on Saturday.

In Edmonton, the city has been under extreme weather measures since December 19 due to the cold conditions. A press statement indicated that these measures will be discontinued on Sunday afternoon, as forecasts predict an improvement in temperatures in the coming week. Environment Canada reported that Edmonton's temperature is expected to drop to -26 C on Saturday, with wind chill making it feel as cold as -37 at times. By Monday, temperatures in Alberta's capital are anticipated to rise to a high of 2 C.
