A potential train disaster on the Milan-Lecco railway was narrowly avoided on Wednesday when firefighters successfully stopped a locomotive just meters from a compromised track section caused by a sinkhole. The sinkhole undermined a segment of railway track near Bulciago station in Lecco province, prompting the halt of rail line operations.

The sinkhole emerged as a result of aggressive storms that have been battering various regions of Italy since Tuesday, causing widespread damage and disruption. The severe weather has led to flooding, landslides, and toppled trees, leaving firefighters overwhelmed as they manage numerous emergencies. On Elba Island, approximately 200 individuals were isolated after a landslide blocked a roadway near Forno beach.

