The National Disaster Management Authority had issued a flood alert days earlier, warning travelers of the risks of landslides and road obstructions in northern areas. Officials have cautioned that severe weather akin to the 2022 floods, which inundated one-third of the nation and resulted in 1,737 fatalities, cannot be ruled out.
